{
  "dom_id": "step-q70398",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,3)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x+4)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x+4)$ is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $4$ units to the *left*. So the $y$-coordinate remains unchanged while the $x$-coordinate decreases by $4.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,3)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1-4,3)=(-3,3)$ must lie on $y=f(x+4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214993/assets/2a7333b3778aed3b4a9d744c6a100577fdeeafc497ac9d7f33670908163551b2.png)",
